<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 53 0 R/E(JPFA\220s profitability should hold up strong, even at the trough of the poultry cycle. Feed is priced cost-plus over corn and soybean meal, so the feed segment margin has held in a narrow 6.7%\2059.6% band since 2021, while breeding swung between 3.6% and 25.6%. JPFA also stocks up on corn and soybean meal when prices are favourable. In 2Q26, the worst livebird quarter in years, the commercial farm segment lost Rp 496bn, yet the group still earned a profit to owners of Rp 659bn.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[80]>>
endobj

154 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 53 0 R/E(Feed carries the group through the cycle. It earned Rp 1.9\2053.1tn of segment profit in every year from FY20 to FY25, and in 1H26, which held the worst livebird quarter in years, its margin was 9.6%, the top of its band \(Annex 4\). In our model the feed segment result rises from Rp 4.1tn in FY26F to Rp 4.8tn in FY30F, about 48% of the group total \(Figure 1.5\). Even if the 2027\20528 supply wave and a 25% rise in corn and soybean meal arrive in the same years, profit to owners stays at Rp 2.0\2052.2tn, level with the best year of the old cycle. Signpost: a feed segment margin below 6.7% for two halves in a row.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[81]>>
endobj

155 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 53 0 R/E(Thesis 2 : From Livebird Seller to Food Company)/Pg 11 0 R/K[82]>>
endobj

156 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 53 0 R/E(JPFA is moving downstream to capture more of the margin in its own poultry chain. Management plans to process 40% of its own birds by 2030, up from 15-20% today \(JPFA, 2026d\), and the spending has started: poultry processing and consumer products \(PPCP\) capex reached Rp 459bn in 1H26, more than the Rp 380bn spent in all of FY25. PPCP segment sales rose 29.8% year on year to Rp 6.26tn in 1H26. We project PPCP sales to grow from Rp 10.1tn in FY25 to Rp 37.9tn in FY30F, about 30% a year.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[83]>>
endobj

157 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 53 0 R/E(The shift changes the quality of earnings as much as their growth. Processing earns a steadier 4\2055% margin, and because birds are its main input it does better when livebird prices fall, which is when the farm segment does worst. In our forecast its segment result rises from Rp 0.44tn in FY25 to Rp 1.62tn in FY30F, passes commercial farming in FY27F and lifts its share of the group's segment result from 6% to 16% \(Figure 1.5\). It also ties up less working capital per rupiah of sales, about 0.68x the group's. The ramp needs slaughter capacity, cold-chain distribution and buyers for branded products. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[84]>>
endobj

