<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 55 0 R/T(Macroeconomic & Industry Overview)/E(Macroeconomic & Industry Overview)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

263 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(Demand Grows With the Economy)/E(Demand Grows With the Economy)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

264 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 55 0 R/T(Indonesia\220s economy grew 5.29% year on year in 2Q26, after 5.11% in 2025 \(Figure 3.1\). Household consumption grew 5.06% and government consumption 15.97% \(18.62% for 1H26\), driven mainly by civil-service pay and allowances, with Rp 44.7tn of meal-programme spending in the quarter \(Figure 3.2\). Both feed through to protein demand, and so to JPFA\220s volumes.)/E(Indonesia\220s economy grew 5.29% year on year in 2Q26, after 5.11% in 2025 \(Figure 3.1\). Household consumption grew 5.06% and government consumption 15.97% \(18.62% for 1H26\), driven mainly by civil-service pay and allowances, with Rp 44.7tn of meal-programme spending in the quarter \(Figure 3.2\). Both feed through to protein demand, and so to JPFA\220s volumes.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

265 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(Rupiah and Rates)/E(Rupiah and Rates)/Pg 13 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

266 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 55 0 R/T(Two market prices matter most for JPFA. The rupiah reaches costs through soybean meal, which is priced in dollars. JPFA\220s own balances imply Rp 16,782/US$ at 31 December 2025 and Rp 17,857 at 30 June 2026, 6.4% weaker \(JPFA, 2026b\), and JISDOR stood at 17,611 on 11 September \(Bank Indonesia, 2026b\). Rates set the discount rate. The 10-year government bond yield rose from 6.1% in December 2025 to 7.0\2057.3% since June 2026 \(Investing.com, 2026\).)/E(Two market prices matter most for JPFA. The rupiah reaches costs through soybean meal, which is priced in dollars. JPFA\220s own balances imply Rp 16,782/US$ at 31 December 2025 and Rp 17,857 at 30 June 2026, 6.4% weaker \(JPFA, 2026b\), and JISDOR stood at 17,611 on 11 September \(Bank Indonesia, 2026b\). Rates set the discount rate. The 10-year government bond yield rose from 6.1% in December 2025 to 7.0\2057.3% since June 2026 \(Investing.com, 2026\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

