<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(GPS Imports Signal the Next Supply Cycle)/E(GPS Imports Signal the Next Supply Cycle)/Pg 13 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 55 0 R/T(Broiler supply is set largely by grandparent stock \(GPS\) imports, and changes in GPS show up in the DOC population about two years later \(USDA FAS, 2026a\). The national allocation rose from 530,000 birds in 2024 to 578,000 in 2025 and 800,000 in 2026, up 38% in a single year, and was split among 27 breeding companies against 24 before. JPFA kept 165,000 birds, while state-owned Berdikari\220s allocation rose five-fold \(Figure 3.3\). Our cohort model tracks each batch through two generations of rearing and laying. About 25% of a year\220s GPS reaches final-stock output the next year and 70% the year after, so the 2026 allocation lands as extra supply in 2027\20528 \(Figure 3.4, Annex 10\).)/E(Broiler supply is set largely by grandparent stock \(GPS\) imports, and changes in GPS show up in the DOC population about two years later \(USDA FAS, 2026a\). The national allocation rose from 530,000 birds in 2024 to 578,000 in 2025 and 800,000 in 2026, up 38% in a single year, and was split among 27 breeding companies against 24 before. JPFA kept 165,000 birds, while state-owned Berdikari\220s allocation rose five-fold \(Figure 3.3\). Our cohort model tracks each batch through two generations of rearing and laying. About 25% of a year\220s GPS reaches final-stock output the next year and 70% the year after, so the 2026 allocation lands as extra supply in 2027\20528 \(Figure 3.4, Annex 10\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

269 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(Prices: Volatile Around a Policy Floor)/E(Prices: Volatile Around a Policy Floor)/Pg 13 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

270 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 55 0 R/T(Retail broiler meat averaged Rp 42,577/kg in September 2026, above 2024\20525 levels, while eggs held at Rp 29,819/kg \(Bank Indonesia, 2026a\). The chicken-to-egg price ratio rose to 1.43x from 1.18\2051.28x, which points to tighter chicken supply \(Figure 3.5\). Prices still swing hard. Farm-gate livebird prices fell to Rp 13,000\20514,000/kg in June 2026 \(detikFinance, 2026\), below farmers\220 cost of Rp 22,000\20523,000/kg, before recovering to Rp 24,519/kg in August \(Kontan, 2026\). The producer reference price \(HAP\) is Rp 25,000/kg and the cost floor \(HPP\) rose from Rp 18,000 to Rp 19,500/kg in July 2026, but neither is enforced \(Badan Pangan Nasional, 2024; InfoPublik, 2025; CNN Indonesia, 2026a\). The recovery came from supply action: early culling, lower hatchery output and absorption commitments from integrators. Prices by province are in Annex 12.)/E(Retail broiler meat averaged Rp 42,577/kg in September 2026, above 2024\20525 levels, while eggs held at Rp 29,819/kg \(Bank Indonesia, 2026a\). The chicken-to-egg price ratio rose to 1.43x from 1.18\2051.28x, which points to tighter chicken supply \(Figure 3.5\). Prices still swing hard. Farm-gate livebird prices fell to Rp 13,000\20514,000/kg in June 2026 \(detikFinance, 2026\), below farmers\220 cost of Rp 22,000\20523,000/kg, before recovering to Rp 24,519/kg in August \(Kontan, 2026\). The producer reference price \(HAP\) is Rp 25,000/kg and the cost floor \(HPP\) rose from Rp 18,000 to Rp 19,500/kg in July 2026, but neither is enforced \(Badan Pangan Nasional, 2024; InfoPublik, 2025; CNN Indonesia, 2026a\). The recovery came from supply action: early culling, lower hatchery output and absorption commitments from integrators. Prices by province are in Annex 12.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

