308 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(Two Methods Point to Rp 2,770)/Pg 14 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

309 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(Our target price blends a DCF \(70% weight\) with peer multiples \(30%\). The peer set is five listed integrated poultry producers: CPIN and MAIN in Indonesia, GFPT and Thai Foods in Thailand, and Leong Hup in Malaysia. The blend gives a target price of Rp 2,770, 23.1% upside to the 11 September 2026 close of Rp 2,250 \(Figure 4.1\). Figure 4.4 sets each method\220s range against the 52-week trading band of Rp 1,750 to Rp 2,970.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

310 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(The DCF discounts free cash flow to the firm \(FCFF\) from 2H26 to 2030, starting from the 30 June 2026 balance sheet. 2H26 takes half of the full-year FCFF, or Rp 1,020bn. Processing grows faster than the rest of the group, so two inputs follow its rising share of sales. Its working capital is scaled to its lower capital intensity, 0.68x the group\220s, and its capex is set at 3.3% of segment sales, the FY20\20525 average. Beyond 2030 we use 5.0% terminal growth, with capex back at maintenance level. The terminal value makes up 86% of enterprise value. That weight is high because the group\220s roughly Rp 3tn capex programme in 2026 holds down near-term cash flow. After deducting net debt and minority interests and adding joint ventures, equity value is Rp 35.2tn, or Rp 3,011 per share.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

311 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(The Discount Rate Matters Most)/Pg 14 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

312 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(We discount at a WACC of 10.46%, with equity and debt weighted 61.8% and 38.2% \(Figure 4.3\). Equity is taken at market value at Rp 2,250 and debt at gross borrowings. Cost of debt is 9.31%, the rate on JPFA\220s July 2026 rupiah bond, or 7.26% after tax. Cost of equity is 12.43%, built from the 7.09% 10-year government bond yield and a 6.69% Indonesian equity risk premium. Beta is 0.80, unlevered from CPIN and MAIN and relevered at JPFA\220s capital structure. A regression on JPFA\220s own returns gives 0.79, which supports the choice. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

313 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 56 0 R/E(The target is most sensitive to the discount rate. A WACC one point higher cuts it to Rp 2,290, only 2% upside and a HOLD. One point lower lifts it to Rp 3,470 \(Figure 4.2\). Stressing beta to 1.20 raises WACC to 12.13% and cuts the target to Rp 2,040, 9% below the current price. That beta sits well above both the peer estimate and JPFA\220s own 0.79, so we treat it as a stress case. Solving backwards, the current price implies a WACC of about 11.6%, so the market already prices in a sizeable risk premium \(Figure 4.3\). )/Pg 14 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

