439 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Two Scenarios: Grey Sky and Blue Sky)/Pg 15 0 R/K[50]>>
endobj

440 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Our two scenarios move the drivers behind all three theses at once and rerun the full model. Grey Sky lets the main risks land together: half of the 2027\20528 DOC supply gap reaches livebird prices, corn and SBM rise another 25% in FY27F, in-house processing reaches only 30% by 2030 and the MBG programme is halved. The target falls to Rp 2,410, 7% upside and a HOLD. Blue Sky has the theses play out faster: corn and SBM 10% cheaper than our base path, livebird prices 2 points above CPI in FY27\20528F, a 5.0% processing margin and MBG at its 82.9m run-rate. The target rises to Rp 3,200, 42% upside \(Figure 4.5\). Peer value is the same in both, so the spread comes from the DCF.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[51]>>
endobj

441 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(The signposts under Investment Risk show which scenario is taking shape. A 2027 GPS quota at or below the 2026 level, a wider corn import quota and processing growth above 20% for two halves point to Blue Sky. A higher GPS quota, another rise in corn and SBM prices and falling MBG recipient numbers point to Grey Sky.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[52]>>
endobj

442 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Three Years of Price Paths)/Pg 15 0 R/K[53]>>
endobj

443 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(We then run 10,000 share-price paths over the next three years. Each path heads towards the fair value of one of 1,000 full-model runs, in which the five risks in Investment Risk are drawn at once. Corn, SBM, the rupiah and the 10-year bond yield move as they did over 2019\20526 \(International Monetary Fund, 2026; Investing.com, 2026\). Fair value grows 5.2% a year, our 12.4% cost of equity less a 7.2% dividend yield. Each year the price closes half of its gap to fair value, with JPFA\220s 37% annual volatility on top. The median path passes Grey Sky in July 2027 and our target in August 2029. After one year the median path is at Rp 2,456 and the middle half of paths sits between Rp 2,026 and Rp 2,968. At that point 53% of paths are above Grey Sky and 34% are above our target, while 37% are still below today\220s price. By September 2028 the median reaches Rp 2,620 and 31% of paths remain below Rp 2,250.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[54]>>
endobj

444 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Probability of Beating Each Target)/Pg 15 0 R/K[55]>>
endobj

445 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Paths spread widely by 2029. Leaving out the top and bottom 5% of paths \(Rp 1,567 to Rp 5,009\), half end above our Rp 2,770 target and a third above Blue Sky, while 32% end below Grey Sky \(Figure 4.6\). Against today\220s Rp 2,250, 59% of these paths return 15% or more, the BUY band, 27% fall in the HOLD band and 14% lose 10% or more. Most of the spread comes from the share price\220s own volatility, since half of the model\220s fair values sit between Rp 2,320 and Rp 2,910. Our rating rests on fair value, and the paths show that the market may need more than a year to get there. The paths track the share price only. Holders also collect a dividend yield of 6.7\2058.0% a year while they wait, which adds up to more than a fifth of today\220s price over three years.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[56]>>
endobj

446 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Peers Say the Shares Are Fairly Priced)/Pg 15 0 R/K[57]>>
endobj

447 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Peer multiples use trailing 12-month results to June 2026. The five peers trade at a median 5.8x P/E and 4.0x EV/EBITDA, against 5.0x and 4.5x for JPFA. JPFA\220s discount on P/E and premium on EV/EBITDA reflect its heavier balance sheet, with Rp 13.7tn of net debt against a market value of about Rp 26tn. On JPFA\220s earnings and EBITDA, the peer medians imply Rp 2,615 and Rp 1,825 per share, an average of Rp 2,220. That sits close to the current price, so on relative terms JPFA looks fairly valued and the upside comes from the DCF. Leaving out the highest and lowest peer, the range is Rp 2,183 to Rp 3,115 on P/E and Rp 1,593 to Rp 2,554 on EV/EBITDA. We keep a 30% weight on peers as a market cross-check on the DCF, since multiples show where investors price the sector today.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[58]>>
endobj

448 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 57 0 R/E(Source : Team Analysis \(10,000 price paths\))/Pg 15 0 R/K[59]>>
endobj

