481 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 58 0 R/E(JPFA grew fastest of the six in 2Q26 and is second by sales after CPIN \(Figure 5.4\). Its margins sit a little below the median, because cost-plus feed and commercial farming still dominate the mix. Its 29% ROE is second only to TFG and comes from turnover, with sales at 3.8x equity against a 3.5x median. Debt is the gap. At 1.5x EBITDA only MAIN carries more, which is why JPFA looks cheaper on P/E than on EV/EBITDA. At the December year-end, with less short-term debt, it was 1.1x \(Figure 5.7\).)/Pg 16 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

