701 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(R2 : Feed costs: corn and soybean meal \(T1\))/Pg 18 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

702 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(Raw materials are 90% of JPFA's cost of goods. Corn is half of its feed formula and soybean meal \(SBM\) 23.5% \(JPFA, 2026d\), and both prices are set largely by policy \(Figure 3.6\). Feed is priced cost-plus, so the damage lands downstream: feed is 70% of breeding and farm costs, and livebird prices do not follow corn. Repeating the 2025\20526 move in FY27F \(corn and SBM +25%\) cuts FY27F profit to owners from Rp 4.5tn to Rp 2.9tn and the target by 4%, to Rp 2,660. Corn matters more than SBM \(\2122.9% against \2121.1%\), and a partial livebird price recovery, as in mid-2026, would offset the hit \(Figure 6.2\). Mitigation: monthly price resets and imported feed wheat when corn is short. Signpost: the 2027 corn import quota.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

703 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(R4 : Processing ramp slips \(T2\))/Pg 18 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

704 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(R3 : Rates and rupiah uncertainty \(T1, T3\))/Pg 18 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

705 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(Bank Indonesia tightening or a weaker rupiah would raise the discount rate. Our 10.5% WACC uses a 7.09% 10-year bond yield, a beta of 0.80 and a 9.3% pre-tax cost of rupiah debt. A one-point rise in WACC cuts the target 17% to Rp 2,290, a HOLD, and is the largest single risk \(Figure 6.7\). The call turns HOLD at a WACC of about 10.8% and SELL near 12.2% \(Figure 6.3\). The 10-year yield is already at 7.0\2057.3%. Each further point takes about 11% off the target, as equity is 62% of our capital, and a yield near 7.7%, last seen in April 2020, would make it a HOLD. A further 10% fall in the rupiah adds about 2.4% to raw-material costs through SBM, which feed prices pass on. Mitigation: net US-dollar liabilities fell to US$68m after the March bond repayment \(Figure 5.9\). Signpost: the 10-year yield above 7.5%, and USD/IDR above 19,000.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

706 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(Source : Team Analysis \(full model reruns\))/Pg 18 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

