endobj

715 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 60 0 R/E(Thesis 2 assumes JPFA processes 40% of its own birds by 2030, up from 15\20520% today \(JPFA, 2026d\), so processing sales grow 28\20535% a year to Rp 37.9tn in FY30F. That needs slaughter capacity, cold-chain distribution and buyers for branded products, and a delay in any of them slows the ramp. At 30%, processing sales grow 20\20523% a year to Rp 28.4tn, and at 25% they reach Rp 23.7tn \(Figure 6.4\). The target falls only 2.9% and 4.7%, to Rp 2,690 and Rp 2,640, because processing earns 4\2055% margins and the birds are still sold live. The cost lands on Thesis 2 itself. At 30%, processing makes 13% of FY30F segment profit against 16% in our base case. Mitigation: processing capex was Rp 459bn in 1H26, more than in all of FY25 \(JPFA, 2026b\). Signpost: processing sales growth under 20% for two halves \(Figure 6.5\).)/Pg 18 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

