758 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 61 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/A[3004 0 R 0]/Alt(Change in target price under four MBG cases: 2027 budget, five service days, programme halved, programme stopped)/K[10]>>
endobj

759 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(The 2027 budget gives MBG Rp 240.2tn for 72.1m recipients, against Rp 268tn and 82.9m for 2026 \(CNN Indonesia, 2026b\). Our base case already uses 71m recipients, so the 2027 budget only removes the extra 1.3% of broiler demand we assumed for FY27F and takes 0.4% off the target. MBG chicken is about 14% of national demand, and a cut reaches JPFA through lower feed volumes and lower livebird prices. With half of the demand shortfall passed into prices, serving five days a week instead of six takes 1.1% off the target, a halved programme 3.2% \(Rp 2,680\) and a full stop 6.5% \(Rp 2,590\), still at the edge of BUY \(Figure 6.6\). Mitigation: MBG growth is outside our terminal growth rate. Signpost: BGN recipient numbers.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

760 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(R5 : MBG budget cut \(T3\))/Pg 19 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

761 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(Environment: Most Emissions Sit Outside the Gate)/Pg 19 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

762 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 61 0 R/T(Scope 3 makes up 91% of the 8.1m tCO2e JPFA reports, Scope 2 8% and Scope 1 1% \(Figure 7.1\). Coal use ended in 2025, but electrification moved emissions from Scope 1 to Scope 2 without removing them, and Scope 2 rose 7.8%. There is no Scope 2 or Scope 3 target. Scope 3 also carries the currency risk in R3, because 35% of poultry-feed and 57% of aquafeed raw materials are imported. Carbon cost is not a near-term valuation issue. At the legal floor tax of Rp 30/kg, Scope 1 and 2 emissions would cost Rp 22bn, 0.3% of FY26F EBIT. At US$50/t the cost rises to Rp 0.64tn, or 8% \(Figure 7.1\).)/E(Scope 3 makes up 91% of the 8.1m tCO2e JPFA reports, Scope 2 8% and Scope 1 1% \(Figure 7.1\). Coal use ended in 2025, but electrification moved emissions from Scope 1 to Scope 2 without removing them, and Scope 2 rose 7.8%. There is no Scope 2 or Scope 3 target. Scope 3 also carries the currency risk in R3, because 35% of poultry-feed and 57% of aquafeed raw materials are imported. Carbon cost is not a near-term valuation issue. At the legal floor tax of Rp 30/kg, Scope 1 and 2 emissions would cost Rp 22bn, 0.3% of FY26F EBIT. At US$50/t the cost rises to Rp 0.64tn, or 8% \(Figure 7.1\).)/Pg 19 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

763 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(Social: Safety Is the Weak Point)/Pg 19 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

764 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(Safety is the main social risk \(Figure 7.2\). Two employees died in 2025, contractor accidents rose from 51 to 141, and the employee accident rate stood at 5.40 per million hours, 2.6x its 2022 level. Closed-house conversion lifts partner-farm productivity, but many open-house farmers left the scheme in 2025 \(JPFA, 2026a\), and they are the smallholders the price floor and the MBG absorption scheme are meant to protect.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

765 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(ESG Analysis)/Pg 19 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

766 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(Governance: The Segment Accounts Rest on Transfer Prices)/Pg 19 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

767 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 61 0 R/E(A 56.3% controlling shareholder and large intra-group sales, with more than half of feed and DOC sold inside the group, make the segment accounts only as reliable as the transfer-pricing policy. Two of five commissioners are independent, above the 30% OJK minimum. Related-party sales jumped to 2.65% of net sales in 1H26 from 0.19% a year earlier, and raw-material purchases from Annona, a sister company, equalled 7.7% \(Figure 7.3\).)/Pg 19 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

