786 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Figure 7.4 ESG Ratings: JPFA vs Its Five Valuation Peers)/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

787 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(We benchmark JPFA against the median of the five valuation peers on four raters \(Figure 7.4\). The result depends on the method. Morningstar Sustainalytics scores unmanaged risk, and JPFA's 42.6 is in the severe band and slightly worse than the peer median of 41.0. LSEG scores reported ESG performance, and JPFA's 2.0 out of 5 is above the peer median of 1.8 and ranks 267th of 435 food and tobacco companies. MSCI \(B against CCC\) and S&P Global \(39 against 21\) both rate JPFA above CPIN, the only peer with a public rating from either.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

788 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Sustainalytics leans on sector exposure, and all six companies sit in its high or severe bands. We therefore read JPFA as average for a meat producer, with better disclosure than its closest local rival. We do not add an ESG premium to the WACC. Two issues could change that view: workplace safety, after two employee deaths in 2025, and related-party trade, which we will check in each half-year report. Our pillar scorecard and ESG data are in Annexes 14 and 15.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

