838 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(We initiate coverage of JPFA with a BUY and a target price of Rp 2,770, 23.1% above the 11 September 2026 close of Rp 2,250. At 5.0x FY26F earnings and a dividend yield of 6.7\2058.0%, the shares are priced as if profit were going back to the Rp 0.9\2052.0tn of FY20\205FY23. JPFA earned Rp 4.0tn in FY25 and Rp 2.5tn in 1H26 alone, and we forecast Rp 4.4\2055.3tn a year to FY30F. The 11.6% WACC implied by the share price, against our 10.46%, shows how much doubt the market still holds.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[55]>>
endobj

839 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Our three theses explain why we think that doubt is too large. Feed is priced cost-plus and earns about 48% of the group's segment result, so JPFA stays profitable even if the supply wave and a 25% rise in corn and soybean meal arrive together \(Thesis 1\). Processing lifts its share of segment result from 6% to 16% by FY30F and earns a steadier margin than farming \(Thesis 2\). With net debt at or below 1.0x EBITDA, earnings at the new level are worth more than the old-cycle multiple the market pays for them \(Thesis 3\). On ESG, JPFA rates close to its peers, and safety is the area that most needs to improve.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[56]>>
endobj

840 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(The call holds in most of what can go wrong. No single operating risk takes the target below the BUY threshold of Rp 2,588, and Grey Sky, with the main risks landing together, still gives Rp 2,410, above today's price \(Figure 8.1\). The discount rate is the exception. One point more on the WACC gives Rp 2,290 and a HOLD \(Figure 6.8\). The rerating may take time, as the median price path reaches our target only in August 2029, but the dividend pays holders while they wait. The first checkpoints are the FY26 results, for which we forecast Rp 5.3tn of profit to owners, and the 2027 GPS and corn import quotas. Figure 6.5 lists the signposts that would make us change the call.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[57]>>
endobj

841 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Figure 8.1 Target Price by Case)/Pg 20 0 R/K[58]>>
endobj

