endobj

3112 0 obj
<</Title(Retail broiler meat averaged Rp 42,577/kg in September 2026, above 2024\20525 levels, while eggs held at Rp 29,819/kg \(Bank Indonesia, 2026a\). The chicken-to-egg price ratio rose to 1.43x from 1.18\2051.28x, which points to tighter chicken supply \(Figure 3.5\). Prices still swing hard. Farm-gate livebird prices fell to Rp 13,000\20514,000/kg in June 2026 \(detikFinance, 2026\), below farmers\220 cost of Rp 22,000\20523,000/kg, before recovering to Rp 24,519/kg in August \(Kontan, 2026\). The producer reference price \(HAP\) is Rp 25,000/kg and the cost floor \(HPP\) rose from Rp 18,000 to Rp 19,500/kg in July 2026, but neither is enforced \(Badan Pangan Nasional, 2024; InfoPublik, 2025; CNN Indonesia, 2026a\). The recovery came from supply action: early culling, lower hatchery output and absorption commitments from integrators. Prices by province are in Annex 12.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2572 0 R/Next 3113 0 R>>
endobj

3113 0 obj
<</Title(Scope 3 makes up 91% of the 8.1m tCO2e JPFA reports, Scope 2 8% and Scope 1 1% \(Figure 7.1\). Coal use ended in 2025, but electrification moved emissions from Scope 1 to Scope 2 without removing them, and Scope 2 rose 7.8%. There is no Scope 2 or Scope 3 target. Scope 3 also carries the currency risk in R3, because 35% of poultry-feed and 57% of aquafeed raw materials are imported. Carbon cost is not a near-term valuation issue. At the legal floor tax of Rp 30/kg, Scope 1 and 2 emissions would cost Rp 22bn, 0.3% of FY26F EBIT. At US$50/t the cost rises to Rp 0.64tn, or 8% \(Figure 7.1\).)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2572 0 R/Prev 3112 0 R>>
endobj

